## BatteryHealthPage — SwiftUI parity (P4-APPLE · P7)

Implemented a native SwiftUI parity of `web/src/features/battery/pages/BatteryHealthPage.tsx`, adaptive across macOS + iOS, as **15 files** under `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Battery/` (14 `.swift` + 1 per-surface `.strings` table), following the repo's established seam/projector convention (mirroring `BatteryTab`).

**Architecture**
- `@Observable BatteryHealthPageModel` + `BatteryHealthPageSource` seam (P1/S8); no networking in views.
- Pure, SwiftUI-free `BatteryHealthProjector` reproducing the web numeric pipeline verbatim (conversions, `fmtNumber/fmtPercent/fmtInt`, insights, recommendations, prediction/range/charge-distribution series, AC/DC breakdown, new-vs-now). SI on disk; display conversion only at the render boundary.
- Native **Swift Charts** + SwiftUI shapes (no WKWebView); design-token styling (`Color.TS`/`Font.TS`/`TSSpacing`…); full i18n, a11y, dark mode, Dynamic Type, ADR-013 staleness.
- Registered on the `.energy` route (`/battery` → `.energy`) via `BatteryHealthRouteRegistration`, wired in `TeslaSyncApp.swift` + `project.yml` + `.swiftlint.yml`.

**Parity: 147/147** — 27 panels, 11 charts (4 RadialGauge, ComposedChart, AreaChart, BarChart, PieChart, 3 ChartContainer), 4 data states, 105 web i18n keys ported verbatim.

**Verification (what ran)**
- `swiftlint --strict` → **0 violations**
- `check-placeholders.ps1` → **PLACEHOLDER_COUNT=0**
- `swiftc -typecheck` (Swift 6) of the 6 Foundation-only logic files → **clean**; all 14 files parse
- `xcodegen generate` validates the `project.yml` wiring

**Gate status: BLOCKED (honest).** `xcodebuild` build/test cannot run — this environment has only Command Line Tools, no Xcode. Per the prompt, that makes the terminal state `STATUS=BLOCKED`, recorded in `.github/prompts/monorepo/logs/apple-page-battery-BatteryHealthPage.log` (EXIT=1, PARITY_COVERED=147). No red was reported as green.

